# arch/os/macos/entropy — the entropy system call, without a C library.
#
# The sibling of arch/os/macos/io: one _sys_ name for the call a program draws
# randomness with, made the same freestanding way and for the same reason, so an
# object with no library under it can still draw some and can fall back here
# when the symbol it wraps is unresolved. The name is getrandom's because that
# is what the callers are written against; the call underneath is getentropy(2),
# which is what this kernel has. -fno-builtin and -fno-stack-protector as io is
# built, so the compiler turns none of this back into a call into the library
# this tree does not link.
obj-$(CONFIG_OS_ENTROPY) += entropy.o

ccflags-y += -fno-builtin -fno-stack-protector
